Chapter: TestSelfVerifyScript

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Shell chapter ShellTypes
  cites Shell chapter ShellBuild
  cites Shell chapter Pipeline
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit

 We say:

 THE FOURTEENTH GENERATOR ON THE PIPELINE MODEL (PipelineModel.md). The emitted
 script is byte-identical to the one that shipped before the migration.

 ONE REFUSAL HERE IS A THROW AND NOT AN EXIT. A missing seed raises `ScThrow`,
 which ends the script without an exit code this model can name: `PipeOutcome`
 spells exit codes only. The stage below says so in its `ps-why` rather than
 leaving the reader to infer it from an empty verdict list.

Section: Parameters

  default-seed : ShellExpr = SePathJoin SeScriptRoot (SeLit "..\\seed\\Codex.cdx")

  selfverify-params : List ShellParam = [sh-param-default "Seed" SptString default-seed, sh-param-default "Kernel" SptString default-seed, sh-param-optional "AllowStaleKernel" SptSwitch, sh-param-default "PCore" SptInt (SeInt 1)]

 `Kernel` defaults to the depot seed and NOT to `compile.ps1`'s default, which
 is `build-output\bare-metal\Codex.cdx`, whichever compiler ran last. A
 build-output kernel is refused only when its digest differs from the seed under
 test, because staging one there is what the gate does.

Section: The pipeline, declared before it is spelled

  compile-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "compile", pa-kind = PkFile, pa-expr = SeVar "compile", pa-from = Just (SePathJoin SeScriptRoot (SeLit "compile.ps1")) }

  run-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "run", pa-kind = PkFile, pa-expr = SeVar "run", pa-from = Just (SePathJoin SeScriptRoot (SeLit "test-run.ps1")) }

  seed-bytes-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "seedBytes", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "seedBytes", pa-from = None }

  seed-len-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "seedLen", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "seedLen", pa-from = Just (SeProperty (SeVar "seedBytes") "Length") }

  header-bytes-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "headerBytes", pa-kind = PkValue, pa-expr = SeVar "headerBytes", pa-from = Just (SeSlice (SeVar "seedBytes") 0 223) }

  src-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "src", pa-kind = PkText, pa-expr = SeVar "src", pa-from = None }

  tmp-src-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "tmpSrc", pa-kind = PkFile, pa-expr = SeVar "tmpSrc", pa-from = None }

  tmp-cdx-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "tmpCdx", pa-kind = PkFile, pa-expr = SeVar "tmpCdx", pa-from = None }

  tmp-log-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "tmpLog", pa-kind = PkFile, pa-expr = SeVar "tmpLog", pa-from = None }

  tmp-out-art : PipeArtifact = PipeArtifact { pa-name = "tmpOut", pa-kind = PkFile, pa-expr = SeVar "tmpOut", pa-from = None }

  sv-arts : List PipeArtifact = [compile-art, run-art, seed-bytes-art, seed-len-art, header-bytes-art, src-art, tmp-src-art, tmp-cdx-art, tmp-log-art, tmp-out-art]

Section: S01 -- Read The Seed

  seed-message : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "Seed: ") (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "Seed")) (SeConcat (SeLit " (") (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "seedLen"))) (SeLit " bytes)")

  missing-seed : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeLit "Seed not found: ") (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "Seed")

  s01-body : List ShellCmd = [ScSetStrictMode, ScSetErrorStop, ScBlank, pipe-produce compile-art, pipe-produce run-art, ScBlank, ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "Seed"))) [ScThrow missing-seed] [], ScReadBytes "seedBytes" (SePathResolve (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "Seed")), pipe-produce seed-len-art, ScEcho seed-message]

  s01 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "read the seed", ps-why = "read the seed under test; a missing seed THROWS rather than exiting, so no verdict below names it", ps-in = ["Seed"], ps-out = [compile-art, run-art, seed-bytes-art, seed-len-art], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s01-body }

Section: S01b -- Name The Kernel

  s01b-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScRaw "if (-not (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $Kernel)) { throw \"Kernel not found: $Kernel\" }", ScRaw "$kernelDigest = (Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 $Kernel).Hash.Substring(0, 16)", ScRaw "$seedDigest = (Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 $Seed).Hash.Substring(0, 16)", ScRaw "Write-Host \"Kernel: $Kernel [$kernelDigest]\"", ScRaw "if ((-not $AllowStaleKernel) -and ($Kernel -like '*build-output*') -and ($kernelDigest -ne $seedDigest)) {", ScRaw "    Write-Host 'REFUSED: the kernel is a build-output binary and is not the seed under test.'", ScRaw "    Write-Host \"         kernel $kernelDigest, seed $seedDigest. build-output holds whichever compiler ran last.\"", ScRaw "    Write-Host '         Pass -Kernel explicitly, or -AllowStaleKernel if that is what you mean.'", ScRaw "    exit 2", ScRaw "}"]

  s01b : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "name the kernel", ps-why = "refuse a build-output kernel whose digest is not the seed's, because build-output holds whichever compiler ran last", ps-in = ["Kernel", "Seed", "AllowStaleKernel"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 2 "the kernel is a build-output binary and does not match the seed under test; pass -Kernel, or -AllowStaleKernel if that is meant. Spelled inside a raw payload"], ps-body = s01b-body }

Section: S02 -- Header Bytes

 The CDX header is the first 224 bytes and the program is handed it as a
 literal list, which is why it is rendered here as decimal text rather than
 read by the program itself: the program under test must not depend on file
 IO to answer a question about a file.

  header-literal : ShellExpr = SeJoin (SePipe (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "headerBytes") [StMap (SeMethodCall SeItem "ToString" [])]) (SeLit ",")

  s02-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, pipe-produce header-bytes-art, ScAssign "headerLiteral" header-literal]

  s02 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "header bytes", ps-why = "the seed's first 224 bytes as decimal text, to be inlined as a literal", ps-in = ["seedBytes"], ps-out = [header-bytes-art], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s02-body }

Section: S03 -- The Generated Program

  header-line : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "    let header = [") (SeVar "headerLiteral")) (SeLit "]")

  size-line : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "      print-line-uni (\"SIZE: ") (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "seedLen")) (SeLit "\")")

  program-lines : List ShellExpr = [SeLit "Chapter: SelfVerifySeed", SeLit "  cites Verify chapter CdxBinary", SeLit "  cites Foreword chapter Ed25519", SeLit "  cites Foreword chapter Sha256", SeLit "  cites Foreword chapter Sha512", SeLit "  cites Foreword chapter Maybe", SeLit "", SeLit "Section: Body", SeLit "", SeLit "  opening : [Console] Nothing = act", header-line, SeLit "    in let magic-ok = cdx-verify-magic header", SeLit "    in let pub-key = list-slice header 40 72", SeLit "    in let sig = list-slice header 72 136", SeLit "    in let content-hash = cdx-read-content-hash header", SeLit "    in let sig-valid = ed25519-verify pub-key content-hash sig", SeLit "    in let has-author = list-at header 40 + list-at header 41 + list-at header 42 + list-at header 43", SeLit "    in act", size-line, SeLit "      print-line-uni (\"MAGIC: \" & show magic-ok)", SeLit "      print-line-uni (\"SIGNATURE: \" & show sig-valid)", SeLit "      print-line-uni (\"AUTHOR-KEY-PRESENT: \" & show (has-author > 0))", SeLit "      if magic-ok then if sig-valid then", SeLit "        print-line-uni \"THE SEED VERIFIES ITSELF\"", SeLit "      else print-line-uni \"SIGNATURE INVALID\"", SeLit "      else print-line-uni \"BAD MAGIC\"", SeLit "    end", SeLit "  end"]

  s03-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScAssign "src" (SeLines program-lines)]

  s03 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "the generated program", ps-why = "a Codex chapter that checks the seed's magic and signature against the header handed to it", ps-in = ["headerBytes", "seedLen"], ps-out = [src-art], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s03-body }

Section: S04 -- Temporary Files

  temp-with : Text -> ShellExpr
  temp-with (suffix) = SeConcat (SeStaticCall "System.IO.Path" "GetTempFileName" []) (SeLit suffix)

  generated-message : ShellExpr = SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "Generated source: ") (SeProperty (SeStaticCall "System.IO.File" "ReadAllBytes" [pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "tmpSrc"]) "Length")) (SeLit " bytes")

  s04-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScAssign "tmpSrc" (temp-with ".codex"), ScAssign "tmpCdx" (temp-with ".cdx"), ScAssign "tmpLog" (temp-with ".log"), ScAssign "tmpOut" (temp-with ".out"), ScBlank, ScDotNetCall "System.IO.File" "WriteAllText" [pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "tmpSrc", pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "src"], ScEcho generated-message]

  s04 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "temporary files", ps-why = "four temporaries: the source, its binary, the compile log and the captured output", ps-in = ["src"], ps-out = [tmp-src-art, tmp-cdx-art, tmp-log-art, tmp-out-art], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s04-body }

Section: S05 -- Compile And Run

  compile-args : List ShellArg = [SaNamed "File" (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "compile"), SaNamed "Src" (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "tmpSrc"), SaNamed "Out" (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "tmpCdx"), SaNamed "Log" (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "tmpLog"), SaNamed "Kernel" (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "Kernel"), SaNamed "PCore" (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "PCore")]

  run-args : List ShellArg = [SaNamed "File" (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "run"), SaNamed "Kernel" (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "tmpCdx"), SaNamed "OutFile" (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "tmpOut")]

  compile-failed : List ShellCmd = [ScEchoStyled (SeLit "COMPILE FAILED") ClBrightRed True, ScPrintFile (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "tmpLog"), ScExit (SeInt 1)]

  run-failed : List ShellCmd = [ScEchoStyled (SeLit "RUN FAILED") ClBrightRed True, ScExit (SeInt 1)]

  s05-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScEchoStyled (SeLit "Compiling...") ClBrightCyan True, ScRunArgs (SeLit "pwsh") compile-args, ScIf (SeNot (SeExitCodeEq 0)) compile-failed [], ScBlank, ScEchoStyled (SeLit "Running...") ClBrightCyan True, ScRunArgs (SeLit "pwsh") run-args, ScIf (SeNot (SeExitCodeEq 0)) run-failed []]

 TWO GUESTS IN SEQUENCE, never at once: the generated chapter is compiled under
 `-Kernel`, then the binary it produced is booted.

  s05 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "compile and run", ps-why = "compile the generated chapter under the named kernel, then boot what it produced", ps-in = ["compile", "run", "tmpSrc", "tmpCdx", "tmpLog", "tmpOut", "Kernel", "PCore"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [PrGuests 1, PrKernel (SeVar "Kernel")], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "the generated verification chapter did not compile; its log is printed above", PoExit 1 "the verification binary compiled and did not run to completion"], ps-body = s05-body }

Section: S06 -- Output

  s06-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScPrintFile (pipe-ref sv-arts selfverify-params "tmpOut")]

 THE VERDICT OF THIS SCRIPT IS ITS TEXT, NOT ITS EXIT CODE. The captured output
 is printed and the script ends at zero whatever the program said, so a caller
 reading only the exit code cannot tell "THE SEED VERIFIES ITSELF" from
 "SIGNATURE INVALID". That is why the seed path in `CLAUDE.md` requires a human
 or a caller to READ this output rather than gate on the run.

  s06 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "output", ps-why = "print what the verification program said; the answer is the text, and the exit code is zero either way", ps-in = ["tmpOut"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s06-body }

Section: Assembly

  sv-pipe : Pipeline = Pipeline { pl-name = "test-self-verify", pl-doc = "Compile and run a self-verification program that checks the seed CDX", pl-params = selfverify-params, pl-stages = [s01, s01b, s02, s03, s04, s05, s06] }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell (pipeline-to-shell sv-pipe))
  end

